WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:05.440
Hyderabad, India's fourth biggest city,

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:06.989
is fast becoming one of the most exciting

00:00:06.989 --> 00:00:09.673
visitor destinations in the country.

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:12.300
Hyderabadi's are really,

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:14.050
really known for their hospitality

00:00:14.050 --> 00:00:15.250
Its booming tech scene

00:00:15.250 --> 00:00:17.520
is attracting global attention.

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:19.040
It's more like wine when you start

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:21.290
enjoying it you, you really
fall in love with it.

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:22.596
And transforming this ancient

00:00:22.596 --> 00:00:25.573
city into a cosmopolitan hot-spot.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:29.430
It's an amazing time to be in Hyderabad.

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:31.516
Once home to the richest
man in the world and

00:00:31.516 --> 00:00:34.937
the center of the global
diamond trade, Hyderabad is full

00:00:34.937 --> 00:00:38.833
of hidden gems, you just have
to know where to find them.

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:42.325
Three passionate locals
are about to take you

00:00:42.325 --> 00:00:45.567
on a tour of their city,
revealing the secret

00:00:45.567 --> 00:00:48.883
spots where you can
experience the real Hyderabad.

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:03.956
If you want to capture the
vibrancy, color, and sounds

00:01:03.956 --> 00:01:07.500
of Hyderabad you'll need
to get up early just like

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.463
the flower merchants of
Gudimalkapur flower market.

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:17.770
As flowers are an integral
part of Indian life, this

00:01:17.770 --> 00:01:20.883
market attracts buyers and
sellers from across the region.

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:30.833
It's also a favorite spot
for keen photographers.

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:35.040
My name is Saurabh Chatterjee.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:36.633
I'm a travel photographer.

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:42.140
Since childhood I had
a dream to travel and

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:44.903
to take pictures for the
people who can't travel.

00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:47.440
Saurabh has taken his love

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:50.990
of photography one step
further and now shares

00:01:50.990 --> 00:01:53.840
it with visitors by running photo walks.

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:55.390
I like bringing people to the flower

00:01:55.390 --> 00:01:57.900
market because there's
so much happening there.

00:01:57.900 --> 00:01:59.860
It's all about the color of the flowers,

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:01.710
the textures of the flowers.

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:03.600
Also, looking for details and being

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:05.687
more aware of what is around me.

00:02:12.435 --> 00:02:14.120
Also it's interesting
to watch these people

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:17.390
and interact with them and
then you take a picture.

00:02:17.390 --> 00:02:19.450
By joining Saurabh it's a chance to see

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:23.640
this city and its people
through a very different lens.

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:24.830
I have to capture one

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:27.433
particular moment, to freeze that moment.

00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:31.396
Market stall holders here aren't

00:02:31.396 --> 00:02:35.280
just selling flowers, they're
also creating garlands

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:37.920
for every type of
celebration in this city.

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:39.890
The use of garlands in weddings

00:02:39.890 --> 00:02:42.730
is just like in the West
the exchange of rings

00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:45.890
where husband and and wife become one.

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:48.790
Each and every garland is made by hand,

00:02:48.790 --> 00:02:51.383
an art form that's perfected over years.

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:07.460
Saurabh's photos have taken

00:03:07.460 --> 00:03:10.830
him all over India one frame at a time.

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:13.320
But it's Hyderabad's people and iconic

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:15.913
locations that inspire him the most.

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:21.180
My name's Srinivas Kollipara, I'm the CEO

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:24.600
of T-Hub, which is India's
fastest growing start up engine.

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:26.683
I'd love to welcome you all to Cyberabad.

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:29.299
So called Cyberabad is the home

00:03:29.299 --> 00:03:33.560
to Hyderabad's flourishing
Tech and Startup community.

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:37.150
The ambition is to create
India's answer to Silicon Valley,

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:41.420
and it's fast attracting a
young cosmopolitan crowd.

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:43.000
In the last few years there's been an

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:46.630
explosion in the number of
clubs, bars, restaurants.

00:03:46.630 --> 00:03:47.810
Because what we're seeing is Hyderabad

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:50.010
is really becoming a global city.

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:52.237
The building to our left is the building

00:03:52.237 --> 00:03:54.377
for Google and they're currently building

00:03:54.377 --> 00:03:56.126
their largest campus outside of their

00:03:56.126 --> 00:03:58.326
Mountainview headquarters
here in Hyderabad.

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:01.635
But when Srinivas has business visitors

00:04:01.635 --> 00:04:04.823
he doesn't take them to
the newest parts of town.

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:08.273
He takes them to the oldest.

00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:16.570
The street markets of
Charminar in the old city have

00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:20.323
been the beating heart of
Hyderabad for 400 years.

00:04:21.580 --> 00:04:23.228
This was the center of the world's diamond

00:04:23.228 --> 00:04:25.988
and pearl industry during
the time of the Nizams

00:04:25.988 --> 00:04:30.988
who ruled over Hyderabad
from 1724 to 1948.

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:33.570
Near Hyderabad were the famous

00:04:33.570 --> 00:04:36.000
Golkonda mines which
produced some of the largest

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:38.690
diamonds in the world, in
fact the Koh-i-Noor that

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:41.460
is in the crown jewels of
the UK, the Hope Diamond,

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:44.040
which was one of the largest
blue diamonds in the world,

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:46.190
all of these came from
the mines near here.

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:50.575
What that meant was that this
place was fabulously wealthy

00:04:50.575 --> 00:04:54.393
and because of that Hyderabad
became a true trading city.

00:04:57.960 --> 00:04:59.480
The diamond industry may have moved

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:02.520
on but the pearl trade
is still alive and well

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:05.284
giving the city its
moniker The City of Pearls

00:05:05.284 --> 00:05:08.163
attracting buyers from around the world.

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:12.363
Yes sir how can I help you

00:05:12.363 --> 00:05:14.720
I'm looking for some pearls.

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:16.440
And what Srinivas really gets

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:18.324
a kick out of is schooling
his western visitors

00:05:18.324 --> 00:05:21.543
in the age-old art of haggling.

00:05:23.410 --> 00:05:25.460
So how much is this set?

00:05:25.460 --> 00:05:26.790
It's 3,250.

00:05:26.790 --> 00:05:27.623
3,250?

00:05:27.623 --> 00:05:28.456
Yes.

00:05:28.456 --> 00:05:31.440
That's a little high I would say 1,500.

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:33.530
Because that's an original pearl

00:05:33.530 --> 00:05:36.000
and we'll provide lifetime
guarantee certificate.

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:36.937
Okay.

00:05:36.937 --> 00:05:40.940
They're very nice but
I'd say 1,500 rupees.

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:42.822
What's the discount you can give me?

00:05:42.822 --> 00:05:43.655
1,500?

00:05:43.655 --> 00:05:44.488
No.

00:05:44.488 --> 00:05:45.670
I can do some concession for you.

00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:46.850
Okay.

00:05:46.850 --> 00:05:50.133
I will reduce 10% for you, 2,925.

00:05:51.040 --> 00:05:52.540
I still think it's too much.

00:05:53.510 --> 00:05:55.470
I'm sure you can do
better than this though.

00:05:55.470 --> 00:05:57.230
I'd say 2000 rupees.

00:05:57.230 --> 00:05:59.600
No sir, 2,000 would be very low.

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:02.663
So I will do my best,
I will do 20% for you.

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:06.530
So the first thing is start low.

00:06:06.530 --> 00:06:08.260
Then stand your ground.

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:09.820
And be prepared to walk away if

00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:11.320
you don't get the right price.

00:06:12.170 --> 00:06:13.320
So this is a good price?

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:14.153
Yes sir that's a very good price.

00:06:14.153 --> 00:06:16.197
Thank you very much.

00:06:16.197 --> 00:06:18.970
But the best tip of all to grab a bargain?

00:06:18.970 --> 00:06:21.343
Get a local to do the haggling for you.

00:06:24.350 --> 00:06:26.180
And if haggling doesn't make you feel like

00:06:26.180 --> 00:06:29.000
a local then a bone
rattling ride in the back

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:31.093
streets of Begumpet might do the job.

00:06:34.180 --> 00:06:36.210
My name is actually Jaininty Rajgopali

00:06:36.210 --> 00:06:38.080
but most people call me
Jonty, it's a nickname

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:41.110
I got in college and just stuck.

00:06:41.110 --> 00:06:44.400
I think I'm a bit of a nomad,
I belong to a south Indian

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:47.373
family but I grew up in the
northern part of the country.

00:06:49.610 --> 00:06:51.910
I found this a perfect place for me.

00:06:51.910 --> 00:06:53.813
Since arriving in Hyderabad 13 years

00:06:53.813 --> 00:06:57.740
ago Jonty decided to
set up her own business,

00:06:57.740 --> 00:07:00.630
taking people to the
true heart of the city,

00:07:00.630 --> 00:07:04.250
and a place where most
travelers never get to visit.

00:07:04.250 --> 00:07:05.457
Hey Usha.

00:07:05.457 --> 00:07:06.290
Hi.

00:07:06.290 --> 00:07:07.123
How are you?

00:07:07.123 --> 00:07:09.710
The authentic Indian Kitchen!

00:07:09.710 --> 00:07:12.910
Home dining is becoming
very popular with travelers,

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:15.282
but here at Usha's they don't
just come to eat, but to

00:07:15.282 --> 00:07:19.400
learn the secrets and skills
of Hyderabadi home-cooking.

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:20.870
And this is the chili powder?

00:07:20.870 --> 00:07:22.910
And this is the Gundu chili powder.

00:07:22.910 --> 00:07:24.280
Okay, and it's hot.

00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:25.810
Himalayan salt.

00:07:25.810 --> 00:07:26.790
Oh okay.

00:07:26.790 --> 00:07:28.403
This is the Himalayan pink salt.

00:07:31.780 --> 00:07:33.213
Wow, that's a lot of salt.

00:07:34.790 --> 00:07:37.580
So the food here tends to
be a little more spicy and

00:07:37.580 --> 00:07:40.860
a little more salty compared
to the rest of the country.

00:07:43.350 --> 00:07:45.331
You understand how people
cook and what they cook

00:07:45.331 --> 00:07:47.800
with and it does give
you a glimpse of their

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:50.300
life especially if you're
going into a local home you

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:53.900
get to see how they live,
what kind of life they lead.

00:07:53.900 --> 00:07:57.060
It gets you under the
skin of the city as well.

00:07:57.060 --> 00:07:58.720
I have a few friends who come here looking

00:07:58.720 --> 00:08:01.301
for curry powder and it
makes it very difficult

00:08:01.301 --> 00:08:03.741
for me to explain to
them that we don't have

00:08:03.741 --> 00:08:05.960
something like curry powder in India it's

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:08.620
an invention which the British did.

00:08:08.620 --> 00:08:10.960
In fact the word curry
itself doesn't really

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:13.393
mean what it means to most Westerners.

00:08:14.470 --> 00:08:16.280
For example, in this part of the country

00:08:16.280 --> 00:08:18.553
curry literally means just a vegetable.

00:08:20.530 --> 00:08:22.810
This is no five star restaurant.

00:08:22.810 --> 00:08:26.310
But it offers visitors
an even rarer experience,

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:29.423
the opportunity to really
see how the locals do it.

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:34.130
In India we prefer to eat with our fingers

00:08:34.130 --> 00:08:36.230
because we believe that,
one, it tastes better

00:08:36.230 --> 00:08:39.390
you're closer to the food,
secondly when you lick

00:08:39.390 --> 00:08:42.070
your fingers it actually
activates the digestive

00:08:42.070 --> 00:08:44.821
juices so your food also
gets digested much better

00:08:44.821 --> 00:08:47.751
if you eat with your
fingers and you really

00:08:47.751 --> 00:08:50.773
cannot eat some of this
with a fork and a knife.

00:08:54.210 --> 00:08:55.043
Too good.

00:08:55.043 --> 00:08:55.876
It's very nice.

00:09:01.790 --> 00:09:03.630
Across town, Srinivas has a very

00:09:03.630 --> 00:09:06.673
different way for people
to get inside the city.

00:09:07.620 --> 00:09:09.070
One of my favorite places to bring

00:09:09.070 --> 00:09:11.353
people is the Taj Falaknuma Palace.

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:14.920
It's one of the top palace
hotels in the country, and it's

00:09:14.920 --> 00:09:19.773
just this amazingly luxurious,
incredible experience.

00:09:21.850 --> 00:09:23.950
The Falaknuma Palace Hotel used

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:26.040
to be the royal guest
house for the richest man

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:30.483
in the world, Osman Ali
Khan, the last Nizam ruler.

00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:37.033
This is where I come

00:09:37.033 --> 00:09:38.963
for high tea with a splash of history.

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:45.590
Welcome to Taj Falaknuma Palace.

00:09:47.969 --> 00:09:49.850
For those in the know, tea here comes

00:09:49.850 --> 00:09:53.040
with a personal tour with
the resident historian.

00:09:53.040 --> 00:09:55.345
This unique palace took 10 years to build

00:09:55.345 --> 00:09:57.366
and 22 years to decorate.

00:09:57.366 --> 00:10:00.129
The last Nizam of
Hyderabad kingdom who was

00:10:00.129 --> 00:10:04.070
the richest man in the world in 1937,

00:10:04.070 --> 00:10:07.640
he converted this palace
into a royal guest house.

00:10:07.640 --> 00:10:10.083
The likes of King George, Queen Mary,

00:10:10.083 --> 00:10:12.483
Edward the 8th stayed in this palace.

00:10:17.320 --> 00:10:19.260
This is the longest dining table

00:10:19.260 --> 00:10:22.190
in the world with 101 chairs

00:10:22.190 --> 00:10:23.620
The Palace has played host

00:10:23.620 --> 00:10:25.883
to many illustrious guests.

00:10:26.910 --> 00:10:28.560
These are the comments written by Ivanka

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:33.043
Trump when she had dinner with
the prime minister of India.

00:10:33.043 --> 00:10:34.773
That's a really interesting
signature there.

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:38.800
And then you have the Agha Khan.

00:10:40.810 --> 00:10:42.590
But visitors don't need to rely

00:10:42.590 --> 00:10:45.269
on their connections to
taste the high life here,

00:10:45.269 --> 00:10:48.283
just follow the routine of
Hyderabad's former ruler,

00:10:50.972 --> 00:10:54.373
and take high tea on the
palace hotel's terrace.

00:10:58.490 --> 00:11:00.460
It's one of my favorite
places to bring people,

00:11:00.460 --> 00:11:03.610
it's such a luxurious
experience, it's a step

00:11:03.610 --> 00:11:06.033
back in time, it makes
you feel like royalty.

00:11:08.780 --> 00:11:11.230
In a city of seven million people,

00:11:11.230 --> 00:11:13.640
sometimes you need to find a quiet corner

00:11:13.640 --> 00:11:16.760
for peaceful contemplation
and Saurabh knows

00:11:16.760 --> 00:11:19.223
just the spot, Moala Ali Hill.

00:11:26.060 --> 00:11:27.794
Once I was looking for a place to go and I

00:11:27.794 --> 00:11:30.510
found this place on top
of a hill and I thought

00:11:30.510 --> 00:11:32.660
let me come here and
see how it looks like.

00:11:34.810 --> 00:11:37.800
I was so amazed with the
view that I'm getting here.

00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:39.430
And I didn't know how I spent a couple

00:11:39.430 --> 00:11:41.720
of hours there and after
that I've been coming

00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:45.100
again and again to reflect
on myself and the whole city,

00:11:45.100 --> 00:11:48.463
the people who live here
and on my life as well.

00:11:52.490 --> 00:11:54.310
At the top of Moula Ali Hill

00:11:54.310 --> 00:11:58.050
is a 16th-century dargah, a muslim shrine.

00:11:58.050 --> 00:12:00.680
The dargahs reputed
healing properties turned

00:12:00.680 --> 00:12:02.914
it into a pilgrimage site and countless

00:12:02.914 --> 00:12:06.473
devotees climb the 500 steps to the top.

00:12:07.954 --> 00:12:08.787
A very interesting vibe

00:12:08.787 --> 00:12:10.273
when you go to that place.

00:12:11.692 --> 00:12:14.320
People say that their wishes get fulfilled

00:12:14.320 --> 00:12:16.340
when they go there, people come

00:12:16.340 --> 00:12:19.533
from really far irrespective
of their religion.

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:34.550
But praying in Hyderabad isn't all

00:12:34.550 --> 00:12:38.543
about quiet contemplation,
it's a chance to party too.

00:12:40.450 --> 00:12:43.040
And with over 50 religious
festivals in the calendar

00:12:43.040 --> 00:12:46.393
year there's always an
opportunity to get involved.

00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:53.240
Every neighborhood will
hold its own festivities.

00:12:53.240 --> 00:12:55.574
And for Jonty, it's
the best way to immerse

00:12:55.574 --> 00:12:58.280
visitors in the Hyderabad street scene.

00:12:58.280 --> 00:13:00.290
One of the ways we show
our love for visitors

00:13:00.290 --> 00:13:03.300
is wanting them to be a
part of our festivals.

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:05.940
So there's always room for
another place at the table,

00:13:05.940 --> 00:13:08.530
there's always room for one
more person at an Indian

00:13:08.530 --> 00:13:11.390
wedding, so if you want to
get in to the spirit of those

00:13:11.390 --> 00:13:15.100
festivals you just should not
hesitate and just join in,

00:13:15.100 --> 00:13:17.050
we'd be more than happy to welcome you.

00:13:25.111 --> 00:13:26.960
It may seem overwhelming but if you

00:13:26.960 --> 00:13:29.350
want to properly
appreciate these festivals,

00:13:29.350 --> 00:13:33.314
there's only one thing
for it, leap right in.

00:13:33.314 --> 00:13:34.730
I think at the last count Hindus

00:13:34.730 --> 00:13:36.543
have about 40 million gods.

00:13:42.780 --> 00:13:45.930
The most popular festival
amongst the communities would

00:13:45.930 --> 00:13:48.210
be the Ganesh Festival or
the birthday of the elephant

00:13:48.210 --> 00:13:52.693
god and it's a time when the
whole city comes to life.

00:14:05.510 --> 00:14:06.780
Some of the most popular

00:14:06.780 --> 00:14:09.920
festivals last for up to 11 days.

00:14:09.920 --> 00:14:11.612
Today's celebrations culminate with

00:14:11.612 --> 00:14:14.710
the watery immersion of the Ganesh idols.

00:14:14.710 --> 00:14:18.823
A boisterous farewell as he's
returned to his heavenly home.

00:14:22.660 --> 00:14:24.535
It may be the end of the night for Jonty

00:14:24.535 --> 00:14:27.560
but for Srinivas the
night is just beginning

00:14:27.560 --> 00:14:30.513
at one of the most fashionable
hangouts in the city.

00:14:31.350 --> 00:14:33.090
There's an amazing new bar

00:14:33.090 --> 00:14:36.340
you enter your secret
code, you actually have

00:14:36.340 --> 00:14:39.990
to know someone to know
where it is but then you

00:14:39.990 --> 00:14:43.050
walk in and there's this
incredibly opulent, beautiful bar

00:14:46.500 --> 00:14:48.980
where they actually serve
you Ayurvedic cocktails.

00:14:48.980 --> 00:14:51.360
Srinivas is here to
catch up with his friend

00:14:51.360 --> 00:14:56.190
Tejaswini, owner and brains
behind this pioneering bar.

00:14:56.190 --> 00:14:57.840
I love this place

00:14:57.840 --> 00:14:59.190
Thank you.

00:14:59.190 --> 00:15:00.240
So, I need a drink.

00:15:02.420 --> 00:15:04.055
Ayurveda is a form of traditional

00:15:04.055 --> 00:15:08.130
Indian holistic medicine
with ancient origins.

00:15:08.130 --> 00:15:11.010
Ayurveda can be applied to
every area of your life.

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:13.836
It literally is your
food, the way you sleep,

00:15:13.836 --> 00:15:16.330
what kind of exercise suits you.

00:15:16.330 --> 00:15:18.840
So applying it to something like alcohol

00:15:18.840 --> 00:15:21.853
which is traditionally kind of damaging.

00:15:22.880 --> 00:15:24.850
So this is the most beautiful way to sort

00:15:24.850 --> 00:15:27.836
of integrate it without
the harmful effects.

00:15:27.836 --> 00:15:28.710
I don't think anyone would ever think

00:15:28.710 --> 00:15:30.740
about healthy alcohol drinks.

00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:33.520
I know but you know
what Ayurveda was one of

00:15:33.520 --> 00:15:37.893
the first to include medicinal
wines in their repertoire.

00:15:39.690 --> 00:15:41.480
It's based on the belief that health

00:15:41.480 --> 00:15:43.740
and wellness depend on a
delicate balance between

00:15:43.740 --> 00:15:47.883
the mind body and spirit depending
on your unique body type.

00:15:49.938 --> 00:15:51.688
I have to figure out my body type

00:15:52.840 --> 00:15:54.970
Your body type will tell you

00:15:54.970 --> 00:15:56.956
what kind of alcohol
and what kind of mixers

00:15:56.956 --> 00:16:00.020
to put in your drink to balance it.

00:16:00.020 --> 00:16:01.950
And what all this does is it helps

00:16:01.950 --> 00:16:04.433
you wake up fresh without a hangover.

00:16:06.150 --> 00:16:07.580
That's pretty cool!

00:16:07.580 --> 00:16:08.560
Awesome!

00:16:08.560 --> 00:16:11.370
So it tells me I'm Kaffer dominant

00:16:11.370 --> 00:16:12.680
So your body type can

00:16:12.680 --> 00:16:14.513
handle hard alcohol really well.

00:16:16.420 --> 00:16:19.290
So I think I'll order a New Fashioned.

00:16:19.290 --> 00:16:20.360
That's a good one.

00:16:20.360 --> 00:16:21.360
You should try that.

00:16:22.650 --> 00:16:23.873
Can I get a new Fashioned please?

00:16:24.940 --> 00:16:26.800
And hopefully that means tomorrow morning

00:16:26.800 --> 00:16:28.000
I won't have a hangover.

00:16:30.660 --> 00:16:32.740
And whatever you think about Ayurveda,

00:16:32.740 --> 00:16:35.053
it's certainly a fun way
to choose a cocktail.

00:16:36.270 --> 00:16:38.916
It's the perfect end to a
day in the city of contrasts,

00:16:38.916 --> 00:16:43.916
where the old meets new, where
tradition meets innovation.

